---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { JACK_FERRENCE } from '../lib/authors';
import { AFFILIATE_REVIEWED } from '../lib/commerce';

const articles = await getCollection('articles');
const stats = [
  { value: articles.length, label: 'articles published' },
  { value: articles.reduce((n, e) => n + e.data.sources.length, 0), label: 'sources cited' },
  { value: articles.filter((e) => e.data.pillar === 'compare').length, label: 'comparisons maintained' },
];

// The date the no-affiliates statement below was last verified true.
// One date, owned by the page that owns the claim. See AFFILIATE_REVIEWED.
const commercialAsOf = AFFILIATE_REVIEWED;
// Mirrors nextCheckDate() in src/lib/articles.ts, which stamps every
// comparison with a next-check date ninety days after its last verification.
const recheckDays = 90;
---
<PageLayout
  title="About Sublime Pantry"
  description="Who runs Sublime Pantry, how it makes money, and why it exists: sourced, honest answers for home freeze-drying enthusiasts and cottage sellers."
  path="/about"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About', href: '/about' }]}
>
  <span class="kicker">About</span>
  <h1>About Sublime Pantry</h1>

  <div class="masthead">
    <span class="masthead-portrait masthead-initials" aria-hidden="true">{JACK_FERRENCE.initials}</span>
    <div>
      <p class="masthead-name">{JACK_FERRENCE.name}</p>
      <p class="meta">{JACK_FERRENCE.role}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>Sublime Pantry is a home freeze-drying publication. It exists for two overlapping groups: people who want every batch to come out right, and cottage sellers turning a freeze dryer into a small, legal, profitable food business. The name comes from <em>sublimation</em> — the physical process at the heart of freeze-drying, where ice turns directly into vapor under vacuum without ever becoming liquid.</p>

  <h2>How a page gets made</h2>
  <p>Criteria are stated before the comparison, not after it. Every figure is drawn from manufacturer documentation, government data, or university extension publications, and each source carries the date it was accessed. Where sources conflict, the page says which one it followed and why. Where a number does not exist, the page records it as absent rather than filling the gap.</p>
  <p>Research is AI-assisted. Every published page is read, checked against its sources, and approved by a human editor before it goes live. Our <a href="/editorial-standards">editorial standards</a> set out how sources are chosen and how AI is used; <a href="/review-methodology">review methodology</a> covers how comparisons are built.</p>

  <ul class="numbers">
    {stats.map((stat) => (
      <li>
        <span class="numbers-value">{stat.value}</span>
        <span class="numbers-label">{stat.label}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>What we will not claim</h2>
  <p>Sublime Pantry has not bench-tested any freeze dryer. Comparisons here are specification and documentation comparisons, and they say so wherever judgment is involved. Nothing on this site is presented as a measurement we took, and no product is reviewed on the basis of experience we do not have.</p>

  <h2>How claims stay current</h2>
  <p>Prices and specifications move. Every comparison carries the date its figures were last verified and a scheduled next check {recheckDays} days later, both printed on the page rather than held internally. Corrections are logged publicly with what changed and when, on the <a href="/corrections">corrections page</a>.</p>

  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <p>Six things, deliberately narrow: machine decisions, batch troubleshooting, food-specific drying knowledge, storage and packaging, and the economics and rules of selling freeze-dried food from home.</p>

  <h2>How this site makes money</h2>
  <p>Packaging is one of the decisions a reader faces after a batch, so we sell packaging: mylar bags, oxygen absorbers, a bag sealer, and complete sets. Every item is assembled from our own wholesale stock and shipped by us. When a product we sell appears in a guide or comparison it is labeled "Sold by Sublime Pantry" next to the mention, not only here. We have no affiliate relationships, sponsorships, or paid placements as of {commercialAsOf}. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>

  <h2>Ownership</h2>
  <p>Sublime Pantry is an independent publication. Where it sells a product that also appears in a comparison, that ownership is disclosed on the comparison itself, next to the mention — not buried on a policy page.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions, corrections, or a batch problem we haven't covered? <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .masthead { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s3); margin: var(--s3) 0 var(--s4); }
  .masthead-portrait {
    width: 96px; height: 96px; border-radius: 50%; flex: none;
    object-fit: cover; background: var(--brand-tint);
  }
  .masthead-initials {
    display: grid; place-items: center;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 2rem; color: var(--brand);
  }
  .masthead-name { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; }

  .numbers {
    list-style: none; margin: var(--s4) 0; padding: var(--s3);
    display: grid; gap: var(--s3);
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--mist); border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  @media (min-width: 560px) { .numbers { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .numbers li { margin: 0; }
  .numbers-value {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 2.2rem; line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .numbers-label { display: block; margin-top: .25rem; font-size: .9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
